[01/30 15:35:48    777s] <CMD> set_ccopt_property buffer_cells -help
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] Usage: set_ccopt_property buffer_cells <value>:
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] Specifies the buffer cells for CTS. If none are specified CCOpt will choose buffers from the libraries.
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] Cell names may be specified as a Tcl list of names, or as a Tcl list of patterns to be expanded to match names. 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] If set explicitly, CCOpt will ignore any dont_use settings for the cells specified. 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] Different buffer cells may be specified for any combination of clock tree and power domain.
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] To use different buffers for each net type set the top_buffer_cells and leaf_buffer_cells properties .
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] Some examples follow:
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] To specify buffer cells for all clock trees and all power domains:
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s]   set_ccopt_property buffer_cells {bufAX* bufBX*}
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] To specify buffer cells for a particular clock tree and all power domains:
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s]   set_ccopt_property -clock_tree clk buffer_cells {bufX20 bufX18}
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] To specify buffer cells for a particular clock tree and power domain:
[01/30 15:35:48    777s]   set_ccopt_property -clock_tree clk -power_domain pd  buffer_cells {bufX12 bufX8}
[01/30 15:35:48    777s] 
